## 💻 Local Setup Instructions

### 1. Prerequisites
* [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) installed (v18 or higher recommended).
* A [Supabase](https://supabase.com/) account.
* [Ollama](https://ollama.com/) installed on your machine.

### 2. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/shubham-bharatera/projectpro.git
cd projectpro
```

### 3. Install Dependencies
```bash
npm install
```

### 4. Database Setup (Supabase)
Create a new Supabase project and execute the following SQL to set up your schema:
```sql
CREATE TABLE projects (id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(), name TEXT UNIQUE);
CREATE TABLE assignees (id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(), name TEXT UNIQUE);
CREATE TABLE tasks (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  task_code TEXT UNIQUE,
  project_id UUID REFERENCES projects(id),
  assignee_id UUID REFERENCES assignees(id),
  title TEXT,
  status TEXT,
  start_date DATE,
  due_date DATE,
  is_blocked BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
  blocker_reason TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE progress_updates (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  task_id UUID REFERENCES tasks(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  update_text TEXT,
  contains_blocker BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

### 5. Environment Variables
Create a `.env.local` file in the root of your project and add your Supabase credentials:
```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key
```

### 6. Local AI Setup (Ollama + Qwen 2.5)
ProjectPro requires the Qwen 2.5 model running locally on port 11434 to parse chat messages and generate reports.
1. Download and install [Ollama](https://ollama.com/).
2. Open a new terminal window and run:
   ```bash
   ollama run qwen2.5
   ```
3. Keep Ollama running in the background. The Next.js app will communicate with it via `http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions`.

### 7. Run the Application
```bash
npm run dev
```
Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) in your browser to view the application.

## 💡 How to Use

1. **Creating Tasks:** On the Home page, fill in the Context Headers (Project, Assignee, Title, Dates) and type your first update in the chat. The AI will create the task and assign it a unique ID (e.g., `PRO392`).
2. **Updating Tasks:** To update an existing task, leave the Context Headers blank and simply type the Task ID in your message (e.g., *"I finished testing for PRO392"*). The AI will move it to **DONE**.
3. **Managing the Board:** Click "Show Dashboard" to view your Kanban board. Blocked tasks will be highlighted in red.
4. **Generating Reports:** Use the "Generate Report" dropdown in the navigation bar. The AI will synthesize all raw progress updates into an executive summary and a formatted table.
